+
+## Voyage 2 — DOM identity defect (browser-only)
+
+**Blocker resolved:** External browser acceptance suite reports 5 failures: toggle-all mark/unmark (tests 1-2), individual toggle mark/unmark (tests 3-4), and escape-edit (test 5). All share one root cause: `render()` in `js/app.js` does `dom.todoList.innerHTML = ''` then recreates every `<li>` from scratch. This destroys and rebuilds all DOM nodes on every interaction. In a real browser, Cypress holds live element references that become stale after `render()` runs, causing `element-has-detached-from-dom` errors.
+
+**Defect:** The product re-renders the full todo list instead of mutating existing DOM nodes in place. The fix is to update existing `<li>` elements (toggle `.completed` class, set checkbox `checked`) and only add/remove elements when the list size changes, preserving element identity across state transitions.
+
+**Specs authored:** `specs/dom-identity.feature` — 4 scenarios pinning DOM element identity through toggle, toggle-all, and edit-cancel interactions.
+
+**Watchbill updated:** 4 new scenarios added to `watch1`.
