+Feature: Preserve todo list DOM identity across state changes
+  As a user
+  I want the todo list to update in place when I interact with it
+  So that the interface remains stable and responsive
+
+  Scenario: Toggling a todo preserves its list item element identity
+    Given the app has todos "Buy groceries" and "Clean house"
+    And the "Buy groceries" todo has a list item element reference
+    When the user toggles the "Buy groceries" todo checkbox
+    Then the same list item element is still attached to the DOM
+    And the "Buy groceries" todo has class "completed"
+
+  Scenario: Toggling all preserves list item element identity
+    Given the app has todos "Buy groceries" and "Clean house"
+    And the "Clean house" todo has a list item element reference
+    When the user clicks the toggle all checkbox
+    Then the same list item element is still attached to the DOM
+    And all todos have class "completed"
+
+  Scenario: Unmarking all preserves list item element identity
+    Given the app has completed todos "Buy groceries" and "Clean house"
+    And the "Clean house" todo has a list item element reference
+    When the user clicks the toggle all checkbox
+    Then the same list item element is still attached to the DOM
+    And no todos have class "completed"
+
+  Scenario: Cancelling an edit preserves the original list item element identity
+    Given the app has a todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the "Buy groceries" todo has a list item element reference
+    When the user double-clicks the "Buy groceries" todo label
+    And the user types "Feed the cat" in the edit input and presses Escape
+    Then the same list item element is still attached to the DOM
+    And a todo with title "Buy groceries" appears in the todo list
